                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "492a2cab-ae2c-32d2-9c3c-d40b13612b82",
                        "entry_id": "624fd96f-a23c-3a59-a051-eb177023691c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing pity; piteous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59b53b72-35e1-4de7-9d6c-e984e34943aa",
                                "sense_id": "492a2cab-ae2c-32d2-9c3c-d40b13612b82",
                                "text": "An if it please thee! why, assure thee, Lucius, / 'Twill vex thy soul to hear what I shall speak; / For I must talk of murders, rapes, and massacres, / Acts of black night, abominable deeds, / Complots of mischief, treason, villainies, / Ruthful to hear, yet piteously perform'd:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbf0e6dd-0e83-4eef-a2f8-b1862a9bc501",
                                "sense_id": "492a2cab-ae2c-32d2-9c3c-d40b13612b82",
                                "text": "When last this ruthful month was come, / And in Linlithgow’s holy dome / The King, as wont, was praying; [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3cb658cf-660c-3df2-8753-16d778debe8b",
                        "entry_id": "624fd96f-a23c-3a59-a051-eb177023691c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Full of ruth or pity; merciful; compassionate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b616aa4-cc75-40ea-972e-77779f26d5ad",
                                "sense_id": "3cb658cf-660c-3df2-8753-16d778debe8b",
                                "text": "Then he bestowed robes of honour on the nurses wet and dry and said to them, \"Be ye ruthful over them and rear them after the goodliest fashion.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
